Rule 3 (input and other must be broadcast-compatible per-dimension with no zero-size dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1) ∧ shape(v_1, i) > 0 ∧ shape(v_2, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (out must be a Tensor object, not a Python float)
{v_3 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ ndim(v_3)
>>
Rule 5 (out dtype must match input dtype to avoid invalid casts)
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 6 (output shape matches the broadcasted shape from input and other when ranks are equal)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_3) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if shape(v_2, i) = 1 then shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) else if shape(v_1, i) = 1 then shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i) else shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i) ∧ shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
